+# Flutter UI Refresh Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.
+> Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Build a mock-only Flutter UI refresh with a dark cinematic welcome screen, light professional login and signup screens, and a refreshed white app shell with floating bottom navigation.
+
+**Architecture:** Add a focused auth mock flow widget that owns welcome, login, and signup screen state.
+Make `ForkMeshApp` stateful so it can show the mock auth flow before the existing `HomeShell`.
+Refresh the shared theme and shell navigation without changing backend services or feature behavior.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Flutter 3.44, Material 3, Provider, `flutter_test`.
+
+---
+
+## File Structure
+
+- Create `lib/screens/auth_mock_flow.dart` for the mock welcome, login, and signup screens.
+- Modify `lib/main.dart` so `ForkMeshApp` gates the existing shell behind the mock auth flow.
+- Modify `lib/theme.dart` to make the default app theme white-professional while preserving semantic colors.
+- Modify `lib/screens/home_shell.dart` to rename destinations and replace the mobile `NavigationBar` with a floating rounded bottom nav.
+- Modify `lib/widgets/connection_dot.dart` only if the avatar border must match the light shell.
+- Create `test/mock_auth_flow_test.dart` for widget coverage of the mock flow and app shell handoff.
