+# ForkMesh Flutter UI Refresh Design
+
+## Goal
+
+Refresh the Flutter mobile app with a modern, professional mock UI.
+The first-run welcome screen should use the dark premium visual direction from the supplied mobile reference.
+All screens after that welcome screen should move to a white professional theme.
+
+## Scope
+
+This pass builds mock-only login and signup screens.
+It does not add backend auth, validation, account persistence, email verification, or real session handling.
+Tapping the login or signup CTA should enter the existing app shell.
+The current app features remain as-is behind the refreshed shell.
+
+## Visual Direction
+
+The welcome screen uses a black canvas with soft purple and white light gradients.
+It presents the ForkMesh brand, a large bold headline, short supporting copy, and two pill buttons.
+The welcome screen is the only screen in this pass that uses the dark cinematic treatment.
+
+The login and signup screens use the white professional direction.
+They use black primary typography, subtle gray helper text, rounded white input fields, and black pill CTAs.
+The fields should borrow the calm spacing and rounded form style from the supplied auth screenshots, but the surface should be light.
+
+The main app shell also moves to a white professional theme.
+The shell should use white and off-white surfaces, black text, subtle gray dividers, restrained accent color, and a floating rounded bottom navigation bar inspired by the mobile banking reference.
+
+## Screens
+
+### Welcome
+
+The welcome screen should say `Build open, sync easy`.
+Supporting copy should mention private relay chat, repository mirrors, and signed collaboration from the phone.
+It should provide `Log in` and `Sign up` actions.
+
+### Login
+
+The login screen should say `Welcome back`.
+It should include email and password fields.
+It should include a `Log in` CTA.
+It should include a link to create an account.
+
+### Signup
+
+The signup screen should say `Create your ForkMesh account`.
+It should include public node name, email, and password fields.
+It should include the existing Solana payout note from the provided signup reference.
+It should include a terms checkbox for visual completeness only.
+It should include a `Create account` CTA and a link back to login.
+
+### App Shell
+
+The bottom navigation labels should be `Code`, `Chat`, `Activity`, and `Profile`.
+`Activity` maps to the existing notifications screen.
+`Profile` maps to the existing settings screen.
+The selected destination should use a strong black circular icon treatment.
+The bar should float above the bottom edge on mobile and remain stable across tab changes.
+
+Wide layouts may keep a side navigation pattern, but it should be restyled to the white professional theme.
+The existing top bar can remain, but it should look consistent with the light shell.
+
+## Components
+
+Add an auth screen module that owns the welcome, login, and signup mock flows.
+Keep the auth flow state local to the root app widget.
+Do not introduce a router or account service for this mock pass.
+
+Update the shared theme so the app defaults to the light professional palette.
+Preserve enough semantic colors for success, warning, danger, muted text, borders, and sender colors.
+Future dark mode can be added later through a separate theme mode or system-adaptive mode.
+
+Update reusable connection/avatar styling only as needed for the light shell.
+Do not redesign repository, chat, notifications, or settings feature behavior during this pass.
+
+## Testing
+
+Add widget tests for the mock auth flow.
+The tests should verify the app starts on the dark welcome surface.
+The tests should verify tapping `Log in` shows the light login screen.
+The tests should verify tapping `Sign up` shows the light signup screen.
+The tests should verify tapping the login CTA enters the main app shell.
+The tests should verify the bottom navigation labels are present in the shell.
+
+Run `flutter test` and `flutter analyze`.
+Manual visual verification should inspect the welcome, login, signup, and shell views in a mobile-sized viewport.
+
+## Non-Goals
+
+Do not add real auth.
+Do not add persisted session state.
+Do not add dark mode toggle in this pass.
+Do not replace the existing data services.
+Do not redesign all feature screens beyond making them fit the light shell.
